<header class="site-header">
  <a class="wordmark" href="/">{{ site.title }}</a>
  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
    <a href="/new-to-numina/"{% if page.url.startsWith("/new-to-numina/") %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>New to Numina</a>
    <a href="/lore/"{% if page.url.startsWith("/lore/") %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>Lore</a>
    <a href="/mechanics/"{% if page.url.startsWith("/mechanics/") %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>Mechanics</a>
  </nav>
  {#- Two search controls, and only ever one of them visible. The form is the
      no-JS path and the one that ships visible: it GETs /search/ with ?q=, and
      that page reads the parameter. It now carries a real submit button —
      html-validate's wcag/h32 had it on all 58 pages, and "press Enter" is not a
      control a pointer can find.

      The button is the JS path and ships hidden, the way the theme toggle does
      for the same reason: js/search-modal.js unhides it and hides the form, so a
      visitor without JS never sees a button that cannot do anything. It opens
      Pagefind's modal, which is a <dialog> — focus trapped and Escape handled by
      the browser. -#}
  <form class="header-search" action="/search/" method="get" role="search">
    <input type="search" name="q" placeholder="Search…" aria-label="Search the site">
    <button type="submit">Search</button>
  </form>
  <button type="button" class="search-trigger" data-search-open data-pagefind="{{ '/pagefind/' | url }}" hidden>
    <span class="search-trigger__label">Search</span>
    <kbd class="search-trigger__key">Ctrl K</kbd>
  </button>
  {#- aria-pressed says which way the toggle is currently set. It ships false
      and theme.js corrects it on load, because the theme in force is whatever
      the OS says until a visitor has chosen one, and that is not knowable at
      build time on a statically served page. -#}
  <button type="button" class="theme-toggle" data-theme-toggle aria-label="Dark theme" aria-pressed="false" hidden>◐</button>
  <details class="mobile-nav">
    <summary aria-label="Menu">Menu</summary>
    <nav aria-label="Site (mobile)">
      <a href="/new-to-numina/">New to Numina</a>
      <a href="/lore/">Lore</a>
      <a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a>
      <a href="/search/">Search</a>
    </nav>
  </details>
</header>
